{
    "_provenance": {
        "derived_from": "kinder/envs/dynamic3d/tasks/Tossing3D/Tossing3D-o1.json",
        "upstream_repo": "https://github.com/Princeton-Robot-Planning-and-Learning/kindergarden",
        "upstream_commit": "39eb7e084c1d54a69f71abfd7faebef62e4a059e",
        "changed": "bin_init_region x moved from 2.23 back to 2.0, which is exactly the value upstream's own Tossing3D-o2.json still uses. Nothing else differs: blocks_goal_region, goal_state and every object are byte-identical to o1.",
        "why": "In stock o1 the bin and the scored goal region do not describe the same place. blocks_goal_region's raw range is x in [1.90, 2.10], which MujocoGround._create_regions inflates by ground_placement_threshold (0.05 m) per side at load, so KINDER scores containment against x in [1.85, 2.15]. The bin's footprint sits at x in [2.081, 2.381]. The only goal predicate is ['on', 'cube_0', 'blocks_goal_region'], so the bin participates in no check: a cube resting in the bin is scored a FAILURE, and a cube on the open floor short of the bin is scored a pass. Upstream commit 1183de7 introduced this by moving bin_init_region from 2.0 to 2.23 while leaving blocks_goal_region behind; o2 was never moved and still matches. Putting the bin back at o2's placement makes the bin footprint and the inflated goal box coincide to under a millimetre in x and y, so 'in the bin' and 'in the goal region' become the same event.",
        "not_the_default": "hitl_pmp uses stock o1 unless Tossing3DEnvironment(coincident_bin_goal=True) / --coincident-bin-goal is passed. Every number measured on this domain was measured against stock o1, and silently changing the scene would invalidate them."
    },
